@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Unlock Azure costs";
    var deployToAzureUrl = ViewData["DeployToAzureUrl"] as string;
}

<h1>Unlock Azure costs</h1>

<p class="lead"><strong>Who can do this:</strong> someone with <strong>Owner</strong> or
<strong>User Access Administrator</strong> on your Azure subscriptions or management group.</p>

<div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
    <strong>Why consent alone is not enough.</strong> Azure uses its own permission system.
    Accepting the app permissions gives us no access to Azure cost data at all. You need to grant
    our application the <strong>Cost Management Reader</strong> role &mdash; read-only &mdash; on
    the scope you want visible.
</div>

<h2 class="h5">First, find MLCP's object ID</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Entra admin centre &rarr; <strong>Enterprise applications</strong> &rarr;
        <strong>All applications</strong>.</li>
    <li>Search for <strong>MLCP</strong> and open it.</li>
    <li>On <strong>Overview</strong>, copy the <strong>Object ID</strong>. Use the Object ID, not
        the Application (client) ID: roles are assigned to the application's identity in your
        organisation.</li>
</ol>

<h2 class="h5">Fastest path: all subscriptions</h2>
<ol>
    <li>
        @if (deployToAzureUrl is not null)
        {
            <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="@deployToAzureUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Deploy to Azure</a>
        }
        else
        {
            <text>Deploy the MLCP role-assignment template (<code>customer-rbac</code>) at management-group scope.</text>
        }
    </li>
    <li>Choose the <strong>Tenant Root Group</strong> as the management group.</li>
    <li>Paste the Object ID into <strong>Mlcp Principal Id</strong>.</li>
    <li>Review and create. One assignment covers every current and future subscription.</li>
</ol>

<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
    <strong>Microsoft Customer Agreement or partner (CSP) customers:</strong> Cost Management does
    not support management groups for these subscriptions, and purchases such as reservations are
    only visible with billing access. Also complete
    <a asp-action="PricesAndInvoices">Unlock prices and invoices</a>. Until then MLCP reads costs
    subscription by subscription, which is slower and does not include purchases.
</div>

<h2 class="h5">Manual path: specific subscriptions</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Azure portal &rarr; <strong>Subscriptions</strong> &rarr; select one &rarr;
        <strong>Access control (IAM)</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Add &rarr; Add role assignment &rarr; Cost Management Reader</strong>.</li>
    <li>Assign access to <strong>User, group, or service principal</strong> &rarr; search
        <strong>MLCP</strong> &rarr; Select &rarr; Review + assign.</li>
    <li>Repeat for each subscription.</li>
</ol>

<p class="text-muted">
    Cost data may take up to an hour to appear after assignment, because of Microsoft's own
    propagation delay. If you have an Enterprise Agreement, also ask your Enterprise Administrator
    to enable <strong>AO view charges</strong> and <strong>DA view charges</strong> in the
    enrolment settings &mdash; without those, the role alone still returns nothing.
</p>

<a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="Index">Back to connection status</a>
